@kommander 
> Neither Warp nor terminal on macos < v25 support modifyOtherKeys or kitty keyboard protocol, so the macos terminal before Tahoe will never support that and Warp will only work when it supports it, see Warp issues like these:[warpdotdev/Warp#2037](https://github.com/warpdotdev/Warp/issues/2037)[warpdotdev/Warp#2528](https://github.com/warpdotdev/Warp/issues/2528)

Not sure if this is any helpful, but OpenAI Codex seems to have solved this problem in Warp on macOS. When running `codex` directly, I can use `Shift+Enter` to create a new line as well as use `Option+Backslash` to remove whole words in the prompting area. While I probably won't have the time to tackle a PR in the next weeks, I think this issue should might be reopened.

@rekram1-node the command i show above (`opencode debug skill`) to list out the 5 skills that I'd expect to see in the opencode TUI don't show up when i run opencode. I'm specifically trying to use the slash command to see it in the TUI like it is working for me on my other machine. I tried the approach you used and the agent shows the skills, so it must be a TUI issue.

The only thing i can think of is this is my first time trying that skill installer which leverages symlinks so we can use the same skill across agents.

